WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:03.969
Speaker 1: So we've had a lot of bad news
and kind of things to be bummed out about

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:08.340
on today's show, but one thing that really
brought a smile to my face was Joe Biden's

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:13.820
White House press secretary, Jen Psaki, just
not caring anymore when it comes to Fox News

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:19.960
reporter Peter Doocy and pointing out to him
that the jig is up, she realizes that the

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.970
dumb questions Peter Doocy asks during press
briefings are just to try to get one of those

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:28.880
absurd segments on Fox News, where the title
around the bottom of the screen is some kind

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.930
of an attack either on Joe Biden or on Jen
Psaki herself.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.540
And so she's just not going for it.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.720
And Peter Doocy tried to ask this completely
meaningless question, saying, oh, you know,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.720
with Trump it was the art of the deal.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.899
But with Joe Biden, it was going to be this
other thing related to infrastructure negotiations.

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:49.260
And Psaki was just having none of it.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.260
Take a look at this.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.380
Speaker 6: You described the infrastructure
negotiations as the art of seeking common

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.380
ground.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.140
At some point, does that become the art of
the deal?

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.990
Speaker 2: I don't know if you're the professional
here, Peter.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:02.990
You're the TV star.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:04.439
You know, what's the fox?

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:09.119
Kairouan, I'm going to be
Speaker 6: the art of seeking common ground

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:10.500
does take a lot of characters.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.119
Speaker 2: Does it?

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:15.459
Does the art of the of the deal would be OK
with that?

00:01:15.459 --> 00:01:17.469
Speaker 6: Yeah, with the art of the deal.

00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:18.560
I think that's a headline.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.869
Speaker 2: Well, there you go.

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:22.740
I thought of a different kind of deal, a deal
for the working people.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.740
Got it.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.740
Go ahead.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:25.740
So glad we could work that out.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:26.740
Speaker 1: Thank you very much.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:30.150
The feel of Peter Deuce's questions.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:36.909
Is that he's trying to play reporter and Jen
Psaki humors him almost like he's not really

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:44.060
competent, but she just has to pretend to
treat him as if he were a competent reporter.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:49.719
And the really funny thing is I think he's
supposed to be seen as asking tough questions

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:52.520
like what when he does this stuff?

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.700
I think there's a contingent of the Fox News
audience that sees that and says, wow, he's

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.380
really there and he's asking tough questions,
but the questions are so silly and childish

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:11.360
and not actually serious in any way that Jen
Psaki and even Joe Biden seem to enjoy taking

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.550
questions from Peter.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:17.090
Like if it were actually the case that this
guy was asking such tough questions and putting

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.921
them in such difficult positions, they wouldn't
be so eager to hear from him.

00:02:20.921 --> 00:02:23.600
They almost seem entertained by it.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:29.380
And it's almost a curiosity to see what flaccid
nonsense Peter Doocy is going to come up with

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:30.380
next.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:34.420
And you get the feeling that Jen Psaki treats
Peter Doocy and in some cases that Newsmax

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.510
reporter named Emerald, who was in the room
last week or the week before, she's sort of

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.450
treating them like you treat one of your kids
when they're having a temper tantrum and she

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.700
has young kids.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.710
You humor it.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:50.230
You allow them to say the thing they want
to say and then you move on while showing

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.040
that it's not really something mommy is impressed
with.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.800
And that's that's the vibe I get from Jen
Psaki during these moments.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.850
Now, after this failed, Peter Doocy tries
again, apparently with a, quote, real question.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.620
It doesn't really go much better.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.620
It's almost sometimes when he's reading his
questions like he's struggling to understand

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.290
because the emphasis and the syntax seems
strange.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.290
I don't really know.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.680
Let's take a look
Speaker 6: quickly on immigration.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.850
The governor of Tennessee says that he was
asked and he declined by the administration

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.990
request to house unaccompanied minors.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:26.920
And in coming days or in recent days, there
have been some reports that at least four

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:32.380
planes filled with unaccompanied minors landed
in his state somewhere in the middle of the

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.380
night.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.380
Can you explain what's going on there?

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:39.470
Speaker 2: Well, as we have been very clear
about children, our objective is to unite

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:44.370
these unaccompanied children, children under
the age of 18 with families, with sponsor

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.370
families.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.420
So children traveling we're traveling through
have been traveling through Tennessee.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.521
They are simply on their way to unite with
relatives and sponsors, to meet sponsors in

00:03:52.521 --> 00:03:56.980
the state or just traveling through Tennessee
until they reach another destination to unite

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.520
with family members or legal sponsors.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:04.410
As you know, geographically, it's right in
a place where, you know, there's a lot of

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.510
states around it.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:09.780
So it's a place where some flights have gone
through as children are moving to other destinations.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.290
Speaker 6: And since this was something that
the governor of the state said he didn't want,

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:19.659
this is not a case of federal officials trying
to sneak something past the state level officials.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:25.110
Speaker 2: I think I'm confirming here that
Tennessee is a state that is right near in

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.509
the middle of the country and some kids have
to travel through there to get through their

00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:29.509
destination.

00:04:29.509 --> 00:04:33.789
And we've been very clear that our objective
is to treat these kids humanely, get them

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:38.349
to safe homes, especially homes of loved ones
and sponsored families.

00:04:38.349 --> 00:04:45.409
Speaker 1: This is an attempt at a new fake
scandal, which is the Tennessee governor doesn't

00:04:45.409 --> 00:04:52.240
want any of Biden's migrant children traveling
through the state of Tennessee.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:57.520
But the Tennessee governor was silent about
this when it was Trump doing the same thing.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.389
This question, of course, ignores that relevant
context.

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:07.639
And yet some flights have stopped in Tennessee
in moving migrant children around.

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:11.990
These are government flights, mostly stopping
mostly at government air bases.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:17.279
And Deucy wants to gin up a controversy that
Joe Biden is ignoring the requests of the

00:05:17.279 --> 00:05:18.830
Tennessee governor.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:24.909
The reality is that a flight stopping in Tennessee
for people to change planes or to reunite

00:05:24.909 --> 00:05:27.849
with their families who may be living in Tennessee.

00:05:27.849 --> 00:05:32.189
It's not really the spirit of what the Tennessee
governor is even talking about.

00:05:32.189 --> 00:05:36.559
And this is, again, mostly the federal government
using their airplanes and airport resources

00:05:36.559 --> 00:05:38.199
available at their disposal.

00:05:38.199 --> 00:05:41.069
But it's supposed to be another scandal.

00:05:41.069 --> 00:05:46.819
And hilariously, they then moved on to this
was being done secretly.

00:05:46.819 --> 00:05:53.309
Check out this headline from a recent episode
of Hannity on Fox News called Biden Administration

00:05:53.309 --> 00:05:56.930
Secretly Flying Migrant Children into Tennessee.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:03.069
Report says now again, secretly, when these
are government planes going to military bases,

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:08.610
airports at military bases, is it secret that
it's just not like, oh, it's United Flight

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:13.930
five from New York to L.A.? To call it secret
is also a stretch.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.400
It couldn't be more deceptive.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:21.550
The reality is that the Biden administration
is just like the Trump administration, continuing

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:25.900
to use geographically convenient airports
around the country for layovers for children

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.189
in their custody.

00:06:27.189 --> 00:06:30.970
And the priority should be reuniting those
kids with their families, which, by the way,

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:37.539
the number of kids who have not yet been reunited
is down 84 percent last month under the Biden

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:38.539
administration.

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:39.710
It's not yet a victory.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.909
Immigration has not been solved.

00:06:40.909 --> 00:06:42.400
DACA has not been dealt with.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.370
But this is at least some progress from what
we were seeing under the Trump administration

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.319
administration, the reuniting.

00:06:49.319 --> 00:06:53.729
Of the children with their families might
most conveniently be done in Tennessee or

00:06:53.729 --> 00:06:54.789
with a layover in Tennessee.

00:06:54.789 --> 00:06:56.090
It's very simple.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.949
Everything is a scandal now.

00:06:57.949 --> 00:07:05.199
And of course, unfortunately, none of them
are really catching on as scandals.

00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:10.270
But it doesn't matter because there's this
general idea from the right, if you watch

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:15.669
Fox News that Joe Biden is beleaguered and
riddled in scandal individually.

00:07:15.669 --> 00:07:18.039
None of the scandals really catch on.

00:07:18.039 --> 00:07:22.749
But you still are starting to see reflected
in polling the idea that Biden is just embroiled

00:07:22.749 --> 00:07:26.210
in scandal among Fox News viewers and Republican
voters.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.389
So this stuff works.

00:07:27.389 --> 00:07:29.180
There's a reason why they keep doing this
stuff.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:31.449
You and I might see it and say another fake
scandal.

00:07:31.449 --> 00:07:32.619
This is trash.

00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:33.800
This is meaningless.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.080
It actually does work to convince a lot of
people

